    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.2.1 Ensure update server certificate key fingerprints are configured"
      info        : "FreeBSD downloads binary updates from an update server and uses Public Key Infrastructure to verify the downloads. This key fingerprint is used in the file /etc/freebsd-update.conf . This key fingerprint varies between different versions of FreeBSD and must be validated manually.

Ensure that updates are obtained from a valid source to protect against spoofing that could lead to the inadvertent installation of malware on the system. Verify the key fingerprint being used is correctly configured in the file /etc/freebsd-update.conf.

NOTE: Nessus has provided the target output to assist in reviewing the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
      solution    : "If the previous outputs of the commands are not identical, there is a high possibility that something is wrong with the system. The verification of certificates might fail for various reasons, but the most common issue is improper date and time. Or in case the version of FreeBSD is too old and the specific running version has not been updated for a long time. Check the date and time before proceeding further.

Impact:

By downloading updates from the wrong server there is the possibility that someone is injecting malicious content in the base operating system."
      reference   : "800-171|3.11.2,800-171|3.11.3,800-171|3.14.1,800-171r3|03.11.02,800-171r3|03.14.01,800-53|RA-5,800-53|SI-2,800-53|SI-2(2),800-53r5|RA-5,800-53r5|RA-7,800-53r5|SI-2,800-53r5|SI-2(2),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(e),CN-L3|8.1.10.5(a),CN-L3|8.1.10.5(b),CN-L3|8.5.4.1(b),CN-L3|8.5.4.1(d),CN-L3|8.5.4.1(e),CSCv7|3.4,CSCv8|7.3,CSF|DE.CM-8,CSF|DE.DP-4,CSF|DE.DP-5,CSF|ID.RA-1,CSF|PR.IP-12,CSF|RS.CO-3,CSF|RS.MI-3,CSF2.0|GV.SC-10,CSF2.0|ID.IM-01,CSF2.0|ID.IM-02,CSF2.0|ID.IM-03,CSF2.0|ID.RA-01,CSF2.0|ID.RA-08,CSF2.0|PR.PS-02,GDPR|32.1.b,GDPR|32.1.d,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.6.8,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.8,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.32,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.6.1,ITSG-33|RA-5,ITSG-33|SI-2,ITSG-33|SI-2(2),LEVEL|1M,NESA|M1.2.2,NESA|M5.4.1,NESA|T7.6.2,NESA|T7.7.1,NIAv2|PR9,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|6.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|6.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|6.3,PCI-DSSv4.0|6.3.1,PCI-DSSv4.0|6.3.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.3,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|10.2.1,QCSC-v1|11.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.7"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/19044"
      cmd         : "#!/bin/sh

  # Get FreeBSD version and architecture
  FBSD_VERSION=$(/usr/bin/uname -r | /usr/bin/cut -d'-' -f1,2)
  ARCH=$(/usr/bin/uname -m)

  echo \"=== FreeBSD Update Server Certificate Verification ===\"
  echo \"System: ${FBSD_VERSION} ${ARCH}\"
  echo

  # Check if freebsd-update.conf exists and show current KeyPrint
  if [ -f /etc/freebsd-update.conf ]; then
  echo \"Current KeyPrint configuration:\"
  /usr/bin/grep KeyPrint /etc/freebsd-update.conf | /usr/bin/head -5
  echo

  # Extract just the hash for comparison
  CURRENT_HASH=$(/usr/bin/grep KeyPrint /etc/freebsd-update.conf | /usr/bin/cut -f 2 -w | /usr/bin/head -1)
  echo \"Current KeyPrint Hash: ${CURRENT_HASH}\"
  else
  echo \"ERROR: /etc/freebsd-update.conf not found\"
  fi

  echo
  echo \"=== Manual Verification Required ===\"
  echo \"To verify the certificate fingerprints:\"
  echo \"1. fetch http://update.freebsd.org/${FBSD_VERSION}/${ARCH}/pub.ssl\"
  echo \"2. fetch http://update.freebsd.org/${FBSD_VERSION}/${ARCH}/latest.ssl\"
  echo \"3. openssl rsautl -pubin -inkey pub.ssl -verify <latest.ssl\"
  echo \"4. sha256 -q pub.ssl\"
  echo \"5. Compare output with current hash: ${CURRENT_HASH}\"
  echo
  echo \"The sha256 output and KeyPrint hash must be identical for compliance.\"
  "
      expect      : "^Manual Review Required$"
      severity    : MEDIUM
    </custom_item>

