    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CHECK
      description : "6.1.3 Ensure permissions on /etc/master.passwd are configured"
      info        : "The /etc/master.passwd file is used to store the information about user accounts that is critical to the security of those accounts, such as the hashed password and other security information.

If attackers can gain read access to the /etc/master.passwd file, they can easily run a password cracking program against the hashed password to break it. Other security information stored in the /etc/master.passwd file (such as expiration) could also be helpful in subverting user accounts."
      solution    : "Run the following commands to set mode, owner, and group on /etc/master.passwd :

# chown root:wheel /etc/master.passwd
# chmod 0000 /etc/master.passwd"
